  "verdict_class": "CLIP_SUFFICES",
  "verdict": "BF16_orig diverges (so the FP16 issue is not pure precision) AND clip_only stabilises (so no quantisation grid is needed). The stabilisation is driven by calibrated clipping at r_g = k · RMS(h_g), not by the quantisation rounding. Paper C v1 should reframe the C-7 finding as: 'the bit allocator's calibrated range estimate r_g implicitly regularises Mamba-2.8B at long context, even when no quantisation is applied.' This still credits the bit allocator's calibration mechanism, but explicitly attributes the long-context benefit to clipping, not to quantisation. It is a more conservative — and more defensible — claim.",
